// S441 reproducer — addendum-2 S4: `reflect(T)` directly in a `for … of` header inside `^{}` fails E-META-EVAL-001.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/site-reflect-in-for-of-header-not-rewritten.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: §22.4.2 "`reflect()` is the single, unified API … The programmer always writes `reflect(expr)`
//           regardless of whether the argument is known at compile time"; a compile-time constant
//           (`reflect(User)`) is a "Direct registry lookup inlined at compile time".
// Actual:   exit 1 `error [E-META-EVAL-001]: Compile-time meta evaluation failed: Signup is not defined`.
//           Control: `const info = reflect(Signup)` then `for (const field of info.fields)` → exit 0.
//           Locus guess (agent-located-verify): compiler/src/meta-eval.ts rewriteReflectCalls
//           (bare type name → string) is not applied to the for-of iterable expression.
<program>
type Signup:struct = {
  email:    string,
  name:     string
}
<form>
  ^{
    for (const field of reflect(Signup).fields) {
      emit(`<label>${field.name} <input type="text" name="${field.name}"></label>`)
    }
  }
</form>
</program>
